{
  "_comment": "PLAN-TWO-MAPS item 8 (docs/progress/two-maps-item-8-ai-anchors.md) -- Arena's own AI patrol hub/core-point topology for yard, raw-decoded from the excluded TeamFight_AI scene (tools/extract/extract_ai_anchors.py). Loaded at raid start by ArenaMapPort.Client/AiAnchors.cs in place of AICorePointFallback/PatrolWayFallback's NavMesh-derived synthesis; a missing/invalid file (any map without a sidecar) keeps that synthesis unchanged. No connection/edge data: AICorePoint.ConnectionsAtNet is never populated outside the Unity Editor's own Gizmos callbacks (see extract_ai_anchors.py's module docstring), so every authored core point here has empty connections, same as today's single synthetic point. 11 bot born points, 43 AIMinePoints (AI data, not minefields) and a census of the scene's far-field leftovers (beyond 400 m of the play area, never exported) are recorded beside them. The census also counts the transforms more than 2 m under the floor (y 6.15) and those outside the play area: Arena's 2,696 bearing points lie 3 to 6 m beneath the floor (near the world origin, not hundreds of metres away) and are never exported (PLAN-YARD item 8).",
